ay, friday, saturday and sunday: from 10:00 to 17:00"]},"date_start":"2022-05-10","date_end":"2023-01-22","is_also_by_appointment":false}],"closing_days":["2022-12-25","2023-01-01"],"prices":[{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Normal"},"nl":{"name":"Normaal"},"en":{"name":"Normal"}},"value":15},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Enfants"},"nl":{"name":"Kinderen"},"en":{"name":"Children"}},"value":11},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Article 27"},"nl":{"name":"Artikel 27"},"en":{"name":"Article 27"}},"value":1.25}],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[],"accessibilities":{"list":[252,255,256,257,259,261,263,265,266],"translations":{"fr":["Accessible aux personnes ayant des difficult\u00e9s de compr\u00e9hension","Accessible","Am\u00e9nagements pour les personnes aveugles et malvoyantes","Am\u00e9nagements pour personnes sourdes et malentendantes","Chien d'assistance","Parking accessible","Accessible aux pi\u00e9tons appareill\u00e9s","WC adapt\u00e9","Brussels Health Safety Label"],"nl":["Toegankelijk voor mensen met een verstandelijke beperking","Toegankelijk","Voorzieningen voor blinde en slechtziende personen","Voorzieningen voor dove en slechthorende personen","Assistentiehonden","Toegankelijke parking","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen","Aangepast toilet","Brussels Health Safety Label"],"en":["Accessible to people with intellectual disabilities","Accessible","Facilities for blind and partially-sighted persons","Facilities for deaf and hearing-impaired people","Assistance dogs","Accessible parking","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids","Adapted toilet","Brussels Health Safety Label"]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-07-21T01:06:21+02:00","published_at":"2022-04-20T15:37:14+02:00","backoffice_id":252270,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.19791107444813},{"id":533611,"date_start":"2022-05-19","date_end":"2022-09-26","date_next":"2022-07-21","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":true,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition"}},"others":{"list":[36,41],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Installation, performance"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Installatie, performance"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Installation, performance"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["nl","fr","en"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Liquefy: Human-Nature","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"\u00c0 travers le temps et les \u00e2ges, la Vie humaine se d\u00e9cline dans son enveloppe physique, avec la force qui nous r\u00e9unit tous.tes, celle de la Nature. Aujourd\u2019hui, ce pouvoir s\u2019oublie au profit d\u2019une vie en soci\u00e9t\u00e9. L\u2019exposition de Moni Wespi \u00abLiquefy: Human-Nature\u00bb, propose de changer de mod\u00e8le de repr\u00e9sentation du monde, en inversant les r\u00f4les. Ce n\u2019est plus l\u2019Humain qui envahit la Nature mais c\u2019est elle qui s\u2019en empare jusqu\u2019\u00e0 les confondre entre eux.\r\n\r\nC\u2019est du 19 mai au 26 septembre dans l\u2019espace public QARTIER de la Station Bourse - Grand-Place, que l\u2019artiste pr\u00e9sente dans les vitrines de nouvelles \u0153uvres, des vid\u00e9os, des photographies et deux panoramas mis en sc\u00e8ne de la 2D \u00e0 la 3D. Au fil des saisons, tant\u00f4t fixes, tant\u00f4t en mouvement, s\u2019y d\u00e9ploient des \u00eatres incarnant de multiples transformations, de leur condition humaine \u00e0 leur genre. Un univers esth\u00e9tique qui nous projette dans une imagerie extraordinaire, issue de la pratique transdisciplinaire de l\u2019artiste. Une recherche hybride, m\u00ealant l\u2019impression textile de surfaces naturelles \u00e0 des d\u00e9cors naturels ou imagin\u00e9s. Avec ce point de vue, le temps d\u2019un instant, l\u2019artiste et la curatrice invitent les passants \u00e0 s\u2019extraire de leur quotidien et d\u2019imaginer une autre \u00e9volution possible. Comme une alter-r\u00e9alit\u00e9, Moni Wespi dresse des portraits de nouvelles identit\u00e9s en concr\u00e9tisant l\u2019acte de transformation et en questionnant les codes op\u00e9r\u00e9s par la soci\u00e9t\u00e9 pour se rapprocher d\u2019un \u00eatre au plus proche de lui-m\u00eame.\r\n\r\nMa\u00eblle Delaplanche\r\n\r\nAvec Zinnema, Bruxelles Mobilit\u00e9 et la STIB et avec le soutien de la F\u00e9d\u00e9ration Wallonie-Bruxelles, commission Culturelle Transversale","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/533611.html"},"nl":{"name":"Liquefy: Human-Nature","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Door tijd en eeuwen heen wordt het menselijk leven uitgedrukt in zijn fysieke omhulsel, met de kracht die ons allen verenigt, die van de Natuur. Vandaag wordt deze macht vergeten ten voordele van een leven in de maatschappij. Moni Wespi's tentoonstelling \"Liquefy: Human-Nature\", stelt voor om het model van representatie van de wereld te veranderen, door de rollen om te keren. Het is niet langer de mens die de natuur binnendringt, maar het is de natuur die het overneemt, totdat ze met elkaar verstrengeld raken.\r\nVan 19 mei tot 26 september presenteert de kunstenaar in de openbare ruimte QARTIER aan Station Beurs-Grote Markt nieuwe werken in de etalages: video's, foto's en twee panorama's in sc\u00e8ne gezet van 2D naar 3D. In de loop van de seizoenen, soms stilstaand, soms bewegend, belichamen wezens meerdere transformaties, van hun menselijke conditie tot hun geslacht. Een esthetisch universum dat ons projecteert in een buitengewone beeldtaal, voortkomend uit de transdisciplinaire praktijk van de kunstenaar. Een hybride onderzoek, waarbij textielbedrukking van natuurlijke oppervlakken wordt vermengd met natuurlijke of ingebeelde omgevingen. Vanuit dit gezichtspunt nodigen de kunstenaar en de curator de voorbijgangers uit om even aan hun dagelijkse leven te ontsnappen en zich een andere mogelijke evolutie voor te stellen. Als een alter-reality schetst Moni Wespi portretten van nieuwe identiteiten, door de daad van de transformatie te concretiseren en de codes die de maatschappij hanteert in twijfel te trekken, om zo dichter bij een wezen te komen dat dichter bij zichzelf staat.\r\n\r\nMa\u00eblle Delaplanche\r\n\r\nMet Zinnema, Brussel Mobiliteit en MIVB, en met steun van F\u00e9d\u00e9ration Wallonie-Bruxelles, Commission Culturelle Transversale","performers":"Moni Wespi, Ma\u00eblle Delaplanche, rue branly, Lucia Gerhardt, Fran\u00e7ois de Saint Georges, Noir Metal, Yoan Robin, Julien Celdran, Pauline Miko, Drag Couenne, Shukri, Pluche, Young Sprouts","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.zinnema.be","email":"info@zinnema.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 555 06 00","agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/533611.html"},"en":{"name":"Liquefy: Human-Nature","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Throughout time and ages, human life is expressed in its physical envelope, with the force that unites us all, that of Nature. Today, this power is being forgotten in favour of a life in society. Moni Wespi's exhibition \"Liquefy: Human-Nature\", proposes to change the model of representation of the world, by reversing the roles. It is no longer the Human who invades Nature, but it is Nature who takes over until they become entangled with one another.\r\n\r\nFrom 19 May to 26 September, the artist presents in the public space QARTIER at the Station Bourse \u2013 Grand-Place new works in the windows: videos, photographs and two panoramas staged from 2D to 3D. Over the course of the seasons, beings embody multiple transformations, sometimes still, sometimes moving, from their human condition to their gender. An aesthetic universe that projects us into an extraordinary imagery, resulting from the artist's transdisciplinary practice. A hybrid research, mixing textile printing of natural surfaces with natural or imagined settings. From this point of view, the artist and the curator invite passers-by to escape from their daily lives for a moment, and to imagine another possible evolution. Like an alter-reality, Moni Wespi draws up portraits of new identities by concretising the act of transformation and questioning the codes operated by society to get closer to a being closer to himself.\r\n\r\nMa\u00eblle Delaplanche\r\n\r\nWith Zinnema, Bruxelles Mobilit\u00e9 and the STIB and with the support of the F\u00e9d\u00e9ration Wallonie-Bruxelles, Commission Culturelle Transversale","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/533611.html"},"de":{"name":"Liquefy: Human-Nature","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/de\/detail\/id\/533611.html"},"it":{"name":"Liquefy: Human-Nature","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/it\/detail\/id\/533611.html"},"sp":{"name":"Liquefy: Human-Nature","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/sp\/detail\/id\/533611.html"},"pt":{"name":"Liquefy: Human-Nature","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/