nslations":{"fr":{"name":"Enfants"},"nl":{"name":"Kinderen"},"en":{"name":"Children"}},"value":0},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Jeunes"},"nl":{"name":"Jongeren"},"en":{"name":"Young people"}},"value":4},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Seniors"},"nl":{"name":"Senioren"},"en":{"name":"Seniors"}},"value":8},{"translations":{"fr":{"name":"museumpassmus\u00e9es"},"nl":{"name":"museumpassmus\u00e9es"},"en":{"name":"museumpassmus\u00e9es"}},"value":0}],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"visit_profile":{"list":[322],"translations":{"fr":["Art Nouveau & Art D\u00e9co"],"nl":["Art nouveau & art deco"],"en":["Art Nouveau &  Art D\u00e9co"]}},"tags":[],"accessibilities":{"list":[252,255,257,259,261,263,265],"translations":{"fr":["Accessible aux personnes ayant des difficult\u00e9s de compr\u00e9hension","Accessible","Am\u00e9nagements pour personnes sourdes et malentendantes","Chien d'assistance","Parking accessible","Accessible aux pi\u00e9tons appareill\u00e9s","WC adapt\u00e9"],"nl":["Toegankelijk voor mensen met een verstandelijke beperking","Toegankelijk","Voorzieningen voor dove en slechthorende personen","Assistentiehonden","Toegankelijke parking","Toegankelijk voor voetgangers met hulpmiddelen","Aangepast toilet"],"en":["Accessible to people with intellectual disabilities","Accessible","Facilities for deaf and hearing-impaired people","Assistance dogs","Accessible parking","Accessible to pedestrians with mobility aids","Adapted toilet"]}},"facebook_link":null,"publication_state":"public","last_updated_at":"2022-07-21T01:35:33+02:00","published_at":"2022-03-08T17:28:23+01:00","backoffice_id":249256,"import_origin":null,"sub_type":"expo","show_in_agenda":true,"ranking":0.244401092453},{"id":520976,"date_start":"2021-10-13","date_end":"2022-08-07","date_next":"2022-07-21","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"fr":"Exposition","nl":"Tentoonstellingen","en":"Exhibition"}},"others":{"list":[36,46],"translations":{"fr":["Mus\u00e9es et art centers","Pluridisciplinaire"],"nl":["Musea en kunstcentra","Multidisciplinair"],"en":["Museums and art centers","Multidisciplinary"]}}},"languages":{"spoken":["fr","nl"],"subtitles":[]},"translations":{"fr":{"name":"T. rex","shortdescr":"T.rex le plus c\u00e9l\u00e8bre des dinosaures\r\nTout ce que vous avez toujours voulu savoir sur le T. rex.","longdescr":"Au-del\u00e0 des images, des films et des mythes, cette expo vous invite \u00e0 une vraie rencontre avec cet animal fascinant.\r\n\r\nD\u00e8s l\u2019entr\u00e9e, vivez un face \u00e0 face spectaculaire avec une femelle T. rex de 67 millions d\u2019ann\u00e9es. Elle s\u2019appelle Trix et vous accueille en position d\u2019attaque. Son squelette, un moulage 3D de haute qualit\u00e9 scientifique, est juste \u00e9poustouflant.\r\n\r\nApprenez maintenant \u00e0 la conna\u00eetre. \r\nLe parcours de l\u2019expo vous propose six premiers interactifs pour comprendre le travail des pal\u00e9ontologues et d\u00e9couvrir l\u2019\u00e9poque \u00e0 laquelle Trix a v\u00e9cu, son \u00e2ge lors de sa mort, son alimentation, l\u2019origine de ses blessures et bien plus encore. Autant de questions auxquelles les scientifiques ont r\u00e9pondu en examinant ses os fossilis\u00e9s et les roches dans lesquelles ils l\u2019ont trouv\u00e9e. \r\n\r\nSix autres interactifs vous permettent d\u2019en apprendre plus sur la pal\u00e9obiologie du T. rex en g\u00e9n\u00e9ral :  naissance, alimentation, d\u00e9placements\u2026 Pr\u00eat \u00e0 relever les d\u00e9fis propos\u00e9s ?\r\nSautez en selle pour d\u00e9fier le T. rex \u00e0 la course.\r\nLaissez votre imagination colorer sa peau.\r\nVivez avec lui le temps des amours au Cr\u00e9tac\u00e9 et s\u00e9duisez-le par une danse\u2026 \r\nGagnerez-vous l\u2019hilarant quizz de la fin du parcours ? \r\n\r\nUne expo \u00e0 vivre avec 12 interactifs-jeux qui jalonnent votre parcours: jeu \u00e9lectro, microscope, vid\u00e9os, quizz, touche -\u00e0 -tout et d\u00e9fis.\r\n\r\nParticuli\u00e8rement destin\u00e9e aux enfants d\u00e8s 5 ans, elle fera le bonheur de tous les mordus de dinos !","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.sciencesnaturelles.be","email":"info@sciencesnaturelles.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/fr\/detail\/id\/520976.html"},"nl":{"name":"T. rex","shortdescr":"T.rex de bekendste dinosaurus\r\nAlles wat je altijd al wou weten over Tyrannosaurus rex.","longdescr":"Vergeet beelden, films en mythes! Deze tentoonstelling laat je live kennismaken met dit fascinerende dier.\r\n\r\nZodra je binnenkomt, sta je oog in oog met een vrouwelijke T. rex van 67 miljoen jaar oud. Haar naam is Trix en ze verwelkomt je... in aanvalspositie! Haar skelet (een 3D-print van hoge wetenschappelijke kwaliteit) is absoluut verbluffend.\r\n\r\nPaleontologen groeven haar op in Montana (VS) en onderzochten haar gefossiliseerde botten en de gesteenten waarin ze is gevonden. \r\nOntdek al spelend en al luisterend in welk tijdperk Trix leefde, wat ze at, hoe ze aan haar verwondingen kwam en hoe oud ze was toen ze stierf.\r\n\r\n\r\nMaar daar houdt de expo niet op. Er valt nog\r\nveel meer te ontdekken over het leven van\r\ndeze toproofdieren uit het krijttijdperk: hoe snel konden ze lopen? Hoeveel aten ze? En welke verleidingsmoves gebruikten ze?\r\nDuik dieper in de expo en ga op zoek naar antwoorden! Spring op de fiets en probeer een woeste T. rex voor te blijven, of grijp een spuitbus en kleur er eentje in! Toon je beste dinodans en verleid Trix!\r\nBen je ondertussen een echte \u2018T. rexpert\u2019? \r\nTest je kennis met een hilarische quiz, als afsluiter.\r\n\r\nDeze tentoonstelling met 12 doeactiviteiten \u2013 elektrospel, microscoop, video\u2019s, een quiz en andere uitdagingen \u2013 is een hele belevenis! \r\n\r\nOntworpen voor kinderen vanaf 5 jaar, maar de expo zal \u00e1lle dinofans plezieren!","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.natuurwetenschappen.be","email":"info@natuurwetenschappen.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 52","agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/nl\/detail\/id\/520976.html"},"en":{"name":"T.rex","shortdescr":"The most famous of dinosaurs","longdescr":"As you enter, you will have a spectacular face-to-face encounter with Trix, a 67-million-year-old femaleT. rex. Her skeleton, a 3D cast of high scientific quality, is simply breathtaking.\r\n\r\nIt\u2019s now time to get to know her. The exhibition includes 6 interactive displays to help you understand the work of the palaeontologists. A further 6 interactive displays allow you to learn more about the paleobiology of the T. rex in general. \r\n\r\nEnjoy the exhibition through 12 interactive stages: an electronic game, a microscope, videos, a quiz, and a variety of challenges! \r\nEspecially designed for children aged 5 and above, this is a treat for all dinosaur fans!","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","email":"info@naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/en\/detail\/id\/520976.html"},"de":{"name":"T. rex","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/de\/detail\/id\/520976.html"},"it":{"name":"T. rex","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/it\/detail\/id\/520976.html"},"sp":{"name":"T. rex","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/sp\/detail\/id\/520976.html"},"pt":{"name":"T. rex","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/pt\/detail\/id\/520976.html"},"cn":{"name":"T. rex","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":null,"email":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/agenda.brussels\/cn\/detail\/id\/520976.html"}},"place":{"id":47,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9um des Sciences Naturelles","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"LE MUS\u00c9UM DES SCIENCES NATURELLES, UN INCONTOURNABLE POUR LES CURIEUX DE NATURE\r\nIci vous rencontrerez les fameux Iguanodons de Bernissart, T.rex, Triceratops, Diplodocus, et 34 autres esp\u00e8ces dans la plus grande Galerie de Dinosaures d\u2019Europe.\r\nMais ce n\u2019est pas tout ! \r\n\r\nRed\u00e9couvrez aussi notre Terre, grouillante de vie, dans une approche \u00e0 la fois esth\u00e9tique, familiale et scientifique de la biodiversit\u00e9 dans la nouvelle Galerie Plan\u00e8te Vivante . D\u00e9couvrez notre \u00e9volution et le fonctionnement de notre corps dans la Galerie de l\u2019Homme. Remontez le temps dans la Galerie de l\u2019\u00c9volution. Explorez la diversit\u00e9 des esp\u00e8ces urbaines dans BiodiverCITY. Observez des sp\u00e9cimens illustrant l\u2019histoire du Mus\u00e9um au travers de 14 chapitres symboliques dans 250 ans de Sciences naturelles. Tremblez devant les terreurs des mers du Cr\u00e9tac\u00e9 dans la Salle des Mosasaures et admirez les magnifiques cristaux de la Salle des Min\u00e9raux.\r\n\r\nEt enfin ne manquez pas les expositions temporaires et toutes les animations du Service \u00e9ducatif : plus d\u2019informations sur www.naturalsciences.be\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Museum voor Natuurwetenschappen","address_street_name":"Vautierstraat","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 52","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Vautierstraat, 29","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"HET MUSEUM VOOR NATUURWETENSCHAPPEN, EEN NATUURLIJKE BESTEMMING VOOR JONG EN OUD\r\nHier ontmoet je de beroemde Iguanodons van Bernissart, T.rex, Triceratops, Diplodocus, en 34 andere soorten in de grootste Dinosauri\u00ebrzaal van Europa.\r\nEn dat is nog maar het begin!\r\nHerontdek onze aarde, die krioelt van het leven, in de nieuwe Galerij Levende Planeet: een streling voor het oog, geschikt voor het hele gezin en wetenschappelijk verantwoord. Ontdek de evolutie van de mens en hoe ons lichaam werkt in de Galerij van de Mens. Stap miljoenen jaren terug in de tijd in de Galerij van de Evolutie. \tVerken de stedelijke biodiversiteit in BiodiverCITY. Ontdek 250 Jaar Natuurwetenschappen aan de hand van 14 natuurwetenschappelijke iconen. Deins terug voor de verschrikkelijke zeereptielen uit het Krijttijdperk in onze Zaal van de Mosasauri\u00ebrs en bewonder de prachtige exemplaren in de Mineralenzaal;\r\n\r\nTot slot mag je de tijdelijke tentoonstellingen en alle activiteiten van de Educatieve Dienst niet missen: meer informatie op www.naturalsciences.be\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Museum of Natural Sciences","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 52","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"THE MUSEUM OF NATURAL SCIENCES: A GREAT DAY OUT, NATURALLY!\r\nIn the largest Dinosaur Gallery in Europe, you can meet the famous Bernissart Iguanodons, T.rex, Triceratops, Diplodocus, and 34 other species.\r\nBut that\u2019s not all!\r\n\r\nThe Earth is swarming with life - rediscover it in the new Gallery, Living Planet, through an aesthetic, family-friendly and scientific approach to biodiversity. Learn about the human body and how we evolved in the Gallery of Humankind and go back in time in the Gallery of Evolution. You can also find out about urban species in BiodiverCITY, discover 250 years of the history of Natural Sciences through 14 iconic specimens, beware of the kings of the Cretaceous seas in the Mosasaur Hall or admire the magnificent crystals in the Mineral Hall.\r\n\r\nAnd last but not least, don't miss the temporary exhibitions and all the activities of the Educational Service: more information at www.naturalsciences.be. \r\n\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Museum f\u00fcr Naturwissenschaften","address_street_name":"rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"https:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be\/de","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nNaturwissenschaften und Naturgeschichte hautnah im Br\u00fcsseler Museum f\u00fcr Naturwissenschaften mit der gr\u00f6\u00dften Dinosaurierausstellung Europas\r\n\r\nVon den Dinosauriern bis zum Menschen: Lust, einem Mammut in den R\u00fcssel zu schauen, einem Dinosaurier tief in die Augen zu blicken oder in die Haut eines Neandertalers zu schl\u00fcpfen? Das Museum f\u00fcr Naturwissenschaften steckt voller Leben... und voller \u00dcberraschungen. \r\n\r\nDie gr\u00f6\u00dfte Dinosaurierausstellung Europas: Die Dinosauriergalerie mit mehr als drei\u00dfig vollst\u00e4ndigen Skeletten und zahlreichen Dinosaurierfragmenten ist die gr\u00f6\u00dfte Dinosaurierausstellung Europas. Nebenbei erf\u00e4hrt man interessante Details aus dem Leben - und Sterben - der Dinosaurier...\r\n\r\nNeuheiten: Die \u201eGalerie de l'Homme\": Neuste Attraktion ist die \u201eGalerie de l'Homme\" - die Galerie des Menschen, die einen faszinierenden Einblick in 7 Millionen Jahre Menschheitsgeschichte gibt. Vom Embryo zum Erwachsenen - entdecken Sie die Entwicklung und die Evolution bis zum modernen Menschen oder den menschlichen K\u00f6rper und seine Funktionsweise anhand von Fossiliensammlungen, 3D-Nachbildungen und interaktiven Pr\u00e4sentationen. \r\n\r\nDer Mosasaurier-Saal: Die Mosasaurier waren in der Oberkreide eine weltweit verbreitete Gruppe von Meeresreptilien. In dem neuen Saal, der sich unterhalb der Dinosaurier-Galerie befindet, haben Sie Gelegenheit, diese \u201eurzeitlichen K\u00f6nige der Meere\" zu bewundern.\r\n\r\nLeibliches Wohl:\r\n\r\nDer Magen knurrt, die Zunge ist trocken? G\u00f6nnen Sie sich eine kleine Pause im Dino Caf\u00e9.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Museo di Scienze Naturali","address_street_name":"rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.sciencesnaturelles.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nIl Museo di Scienze naturali di Bruxelles conserva la pi\u00f9 importante collezione di scheletri di dinosauro d\u2019Europa, ma non solo!\r\n\r\nTroverete molti dinosauri tra cui Tirannosauri Rex, Triceratopi e Diplodochi, potrete ammirare anche la vasta collezione di fossili d\u2019Iguanodonti di inestimabile valore, di cui il Belgio \u00e8 estremamente fiero.     \r\n\r\n\r\nDa non perdere: la Nuova Galleria dell\u2019Uomo \r\n\r\nDal Sahelanthropus all'Homo sapiens, dall'embrione all'adulto: nella nuova galleria del museo potete esplorare l\u2019evoluzione dell\u2019uomo e del corpo umano. Quest\u2019area vi d\u00e0 la possibilit\u00e0 di conoscere i cambiamenti che hanno portato all\u2019uomo moderno e l\u2019evoluzione nel corso di 7 milioni di anni, attraverso fossili, video-ricostruzioni 3D, presentazioni interattive.  \r\n\r\nPer saperne di pi\u00f9 \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDa vedere anche:\r\n\r\nLa sala dei Mosasauri\r\nQuesta sala di recente costruzione, situata sopra la Galleria dei Dinosauri vi permetter\u00e0 di ammirare i \"re dei mari antichi\", i Mosasauri, gigantesche lucertole marine equivalente acquatico dei dinosauri. \r\n\r\nLa Galleria dei Dinosauri \r\nLa pi\u00f9 grande esposizione di Dinosauri d'Europa, con pi\u00f9 di 30 scheletri di cui alcuni interamente conservati.\r\n\r\nLa Galleria dell'Evoluzione\r\nUn'esposizione unica nel suo genere in Belgio! Circa 600 fossili e 400 animali imbalsamati a testimoniare la biodiversit\u00e0 delle specie animali di milioni di anni.\r\n\r\n250 anni di Scienze naturali\r\nUn percorso all\u2019insegna di 20 testimonianze storico-scientifiche.\r\n  \r\nBiodiverCITY\r\nQuesta sala, dedicata alla biodiversit\u00e0 cittadina, offre un'avventura urbana a grandi e piccini. Dagli 8 anni in su.\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Real Instituto Belga de Ciencias Naturales","address_street_name":"rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.sciencesnaturelles.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nDescubre la naturaleza en el Real Instituto Belga de Ciencias Naturales de Bruselas, donde podr\u00e1s explorar la naturaleza y nuestra evoluci\u00f3n y biolog\u00eda en la nueva Galer\u00eda de Biolog\u00eda Humana: desde el Sahelanthropus hasta el Homo sapiens, y desde el embri\u00f3n hasta el adulto.\r\n\r\n\u00a1Pero eso no es todo! En este museo encontrar\u00e1s la galer\u00eda de dinosaurios m\u00e1s grande de Europa, tendr\u00e1s la oportunidad de estudiar m\u00e1s de 1000 espec\u00edmenes en la Galer\u00eda de la Evoluci\u00f3n, sumergirte con lagartos de mar gigantes del Cret\u00e1cico en la Sala de los Mosasaurios, disfrutar de un safari urbano en BiodiverCITY y descubrir 250 a\u00f1os de historia de las ciencias naturales a trav\u00e9s de 14 extraordinarios espec\u00edmenes. Con salas dedicadas a temas diversos como los minerales, insectos(en el Vivarium podr\u00e1s observar entre otros seres vivos tar\u00e1ntulas e insectos palo) y conchas, siempre hay algo que descubrir en las colecciones permanentes.\r\n\r\nVisita la p\u00e1gina www.naturalsciences.be para m\u00e1s informaci\u00f3n sobre las exhibiciones temporales.\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Museu das Ci\u00eancias Naturais","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nExplore a evolu\u00e7\u00e3o do ser humano e do seu corpo \u2013 do Sahelanthropus ao Homo sapiens, do embri\u00e3o ao adulto \u2013 tudo na nova Galeria do Ser Humano \u2013 a nossa evolu\u00e7\u00e3o, o nosso corpo.\r\nMas n\u00e3o \u00e9 tudo! Pode tamb\u00e9m descobrir a maior Galeria de Dinossauros da Europa, voltar no tempo na Galeria da Evolu\u00e7\u00e3o, com os seus 1000 esp\u00e9cimes, mergulhar em conjunto com os gigantescos lagartos marinhos do Cret\u00e1ceo na Sala dos Mosassauros, embarcar num safari urbano em BiodiverCITY e descobrir a hist\u00f3ria do museu atrav\u00e9s de 14 \u201ccap\u00edtulos\u201d simb\u00f3licos de 250 anos de Ci\u00eancias Naturais. Por \u00faltimo, as salas dedicadas aos Minerais, aos Insetos (com um viveiro, onde tar\u00e2ntulas, bichos-pau e outros vos far\u00e3o tremer) e aos Moluscos convencer-vos-\u00e3o que h\u00e1 sempre algo a descobrir nas nossas cole\u00e7\u00f5es permanentes.\r\nNavegue no site www.sciencesnaturelles.be para mais informa\u00e7\u00f5es sobre as exposi\u00e7\u00f5es tempor\u00e1rias","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9um des Sciences Naturelles","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"nl":["Europese wijk"],"en":["European Quarter"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"fr":["Est"],"nl":["Oost"],"en":["East"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":8,"location":{"lat":50.83650849,"lon":4.37649387},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-07-21T01:35:44+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:13+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":47,"translations":{"fr":{"name":"Mus\u00e9um des Sciences Naturelles","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"LE MUS\u00c9UM DES SCIENCES NATURELLES, UN INCONTOURNABLE POUR LES CURIEUX DE NATURE\r\nIci vous rencontrerez les fameux Iguanodons de Bernissart, T.rex, Triceratops, Diplodocus, et 34 autres esp\u00e8ces dans la plus grande Galerie de Dinosaures d\u2019Europe.\r\nMais ce n\u2019est pas tout ! \r\n\r\nRed\u00e9couvrez aussi notre Terre, grouillante de vie, dans une approche \u00e0 la fois esth\u00e9tique, familiale et scientifique de la biodiversit\u00e9 dans la nouvelle Galerie Plan\u00e8te Vivante . D\u00e9couvrez notre \u00e9volution et le fonctionnement de notre corps dans la Galerie de l\u2019Homme. Remontez le temps dans la Galerie de l\u2019\u00c9volution. Explorez la diversit\u00e9 des esp\u00e8ces urbaines dans BiodiverCITY. Observez des sp\u00e9cimens illustrant l\u2019histoire du Mus\u00e9um au travers de 14 chapitres symboliques dans 250 ans de Sciences naturelles. Tremblez devant les terreurs des mers du Cr\u00e9tac\u00e9 dans la Salle des Mosasaures et admirez les magnifiques cristaux de la Salle des Min\u00e9raux.\r\n\r\nEt enfin ne manquez pas les expositions temporaires et toutes les animations du Service \u00e9ducatif : plus d\u2019informations sur www.naturalsciences.be\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"nl":{"name":"Museum voor Natuurwetenschappen","address_street_name":"Vautierstraat","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 52","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Vautierstraat, 29","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"HET MUSEUM VOOR NATUURWETENSCHAPPEN, EEN NATUURLIJKE BESTEMMING VOOR JONG EN OUD\r\nHier ontmoet je de beroemde Iguanodons van Bernissart, T.rex, Triceratops, Diplodocus, en 34 andere soorten in de grootste Dinosauri\u00ebrzaal van Europa.\r\nEn dat is nog maar het begin!\r\nHerontdek onze aarde, die krioelt van het leven, in de nieuwe Galerij Levende Planeet: een streling voor het oog, geschikt voor het hele gezin en wetenschappelijk verantwoord. Ontdek de evolutie van de mens en hoe ons lichaam werkt in de Galerij van de Mens. Stap miljoenen jaren terug in de tijd in de Galerij van de Evolutie. \tVerken de stedelijke biodiversiteit in BiodiverCITY. Ontdek 250 Jaar Natuurwetenschappen aan de hand van 14 natuurwetenschappelijke iconen. Deins terug voor de verschrikkelijke zeereptielen uit het Krijttijdperk in onze Zaal van de Mosasauri\u00ebrs en bewonder de prachtige exemplaren in de Mineralenzaal;\r\n\r\nTot slot mag je de tijdelijke tentoonstellingen en alle activiteiten van de Educatieve Dienst niet missen: meer informatie op www.naturalsciences.be\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"en":{"name":"Museum of Natural Sciences","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 52","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"THE MUSEUM OF NATURAL SCIENCES: A GREAT DAY OUT, NATURALLY!\r\nIn the largest Dinosaur Gallery in Europe, you can meet the famous Bernissart Iguanodons, T.rex, Triceratops, Diplodocus, and 34 other species.\r\nBut that\u2019s not all!\r\n\r\nThe Earth is swarming with life - rediscover it in the new Gallery, Living Planet, through an aesthetic, family-friendly and scientific approach to biodiversity. Learn about the human body and how we evolved in the Gallery of Humankind and go back in time in the Gallery of Evolution. You can also find out about urban species in BiodiverCITY, discover 250 years of the history of Natural Sciences through 14 iconic specimens, beware of the kings of the Cretaceous seas in the Mosasaur Hall or admire the magnificent crystals in the Mineral Hall.\r\n\r\nAnd last but not least, don't miss the temporary exhibitions and all the activities of the Educational Service: more information at www.naturalsciences.be. \r\n\r\n\r\n","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"de":{"name":"Museum f\u00fcr Naturwissenschaften","address_street_name":"rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"https:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be\/de","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nNaturwissenschaften und Naturgeschichte hautnah im Br\u00fcsseler Museum f\u00fcr Naturwissenschaften mit der gr\u00f6\u00dften Dinosaurierausstellung Europas\r\n\r\nVon den Dinosauriern bis zum Menschen: Lust, einem Mammut in den R\u00fcssel zu schauen, einem Dinosaurier tief in die Augen zu blicken oder in die Haut eines Neandertalers zu schl\u00fcpfen? Das Museum f\u00fcr Naturwissenschaften steckt voller Leben... und voller \u00dcberraschungen. \r\n\r\nDie gr\u00f6\u00dfte Dinosaurierausstellung Europas: Die Dinosauriergalerie mit mehr als drei\u00dfig vollst\u00e4ndigen Skeletten und zahlreichen Dinosaurierfragmenten ist die gr\u00f6\u00dfte Dinosaurierausstellung Europas. Nebenbei erf\u00e4hrt man interessante Details aus dem Leben - und Sterben - der Dinosaurier...\r\n\r\nNeuheiten: Die \u201eGalerie de l'Homme\": Neuste Attraktion ist die \u201eGalerie de l'Homme\" - die Galerie des Menschen, die einen faszinierenden Einblick in 7 Millionen Jahre Menschheitsgeschichte gibt. Vom Embryo zum Erwachsenen - entdecken Sie die Entwicklung und die Evolution bis zum modernen Menschen oder den menschlichen K\u00f6rper und seine Funktionsweise anhand von Fossiliensammlungen, 3D-Nachbildungen und interaktiven Pr\u00e4sentationen. \r\n\r\nDer Mosasaurier-Saal: Die Mosasaurier waren in der Oberkreide eine weltweit verbreitete Gruppe von Meeresreptilien. In dem neuen Saal, der sich unterhalb der Dinosaurier-Galerie befindet, haben Sie Gelegenheit, diese \u201eurzeitlichen K\u00f6nige der Meere\" zu bewundern.\r\n\r\nLeibliches Wohl:\r\n\r\nDer Magen knurrt, die Zunge ist trocken? G\u00f6nnen Sie sich eine kleine Pause im Dino Caf\u00e9.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"it":{"name":"Museo di Scienze Naturali","address_street_name":"rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.sciencesnaturelles.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nIl Museo di Scienze naturali di Bruxelles conserva la pi\u00f9 importante collezione di scheletri di dinosauro d\u2019Europa, ma non solo!\r\n\r\nTroverete molti dinosauri tra cui Tirannosauri Rex, Triceratopi e Diplodochi, potrete ammirare anche la vasta collezione di fossili d\u2019Iguanodonti di inestimabile valore, di cui il Belgio \u00e8 estremamente fiero.     \r\n\r\n\r\nDa non perdere: la Nuova Galleria dell\u2019Uomo \r\n\r\nDal Sahelanthropus all'Homo sapiens, dall'embrione all'adulto: nella nuova galleria del museo potete esplorare l\u2019evoluzione dell\u2019uomo e del corpo umano. Quest\u2019area vi d\u00e0 la possibilit\u00e0 di conoscere i cambiamenti che hanno portato all\u2019uomo moderno e l\u2019evoluzione nel corso di 7 milioni di anni, attraverso fossili, video-ricostruzioni 3D, presentazioni interattive.  \r\n\r\nPer saperne di pi\u00f9 \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDa vedere anche:\r\n\r\nLa sala dei Mosasauri\r\nQuesta sala di recente costruzione, situata sopra la Galleria dei Dinosauri vi permetter\u00e0 di ammirare i \"re dei mari antichi\", i Mosasauri, gigantesche lucertole marine equivalente acquatico dei dinosauri. \r\n\r\nLa Galleria dei Dinosauri \r\nLa pi\u00f9 grande esposizione di Dinosauri d'Europa, con pi\u00f9 di 30 scheletri di cui alcuni interamente conservati.\r\n\r\nLa Galleria dell'Evoluzione\r\nUn'esposizione unica nel suo genere in Belgio! Circa 600 fossili e 400 animali imbalsamati a testimoniare la biodiversit\u00e0 delle specie animali di milioni di anni.\r\n\r\n250 anni di Scienze naturali\r\nUn percorso all\u2019insegna di 20 testimonianze storico-scientifiche.\r\n  \r\nBiodiverCITY\r\nQuesta sala, dedicata alla biodiversit\u00e0 cittadina, offre un'avventura urbana a grandi e piccini. Dagli 8 anni in su.\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"sp":{"name":"Real Instituto Belga de Ciencias Naturales","address_street_name":"rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.sciencesnaturelles.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nDescubre la naturaleza en el Real Instituto Belga de Ciencias Naturales de Bruselas, donde podr\u00e1s explorar la naturaleza y nuestra evoluci\u00f3n y biolog\u00eda en la nueva Galer\u00eda de Biolog\u00eda Humana: desde el Sahelanthropus hasta el Homo sapiens, y desde el embri\u00f3n hasta el adulto.\r\n\r\n\u00a1Pero eso no es todo! En este museo encontrar\u00e1s la galer\u00eda de dinosaurios m\u00e1s grande de Europa, tendr\u00e1s la oportunidad de estudiar m\u00e1s de 1000 espec\u00edmenes en la Galer\u00eda de la Evoluci\u00f3n, sumergirte con lagartos de mar gigantes del Cret\u00e1cico en la Sala de los Mosasaurios, disfrutar de un safari urbano en BiodiverCITY y descubrir 250 a\u00f1os de historia de las ciencias naturales a trav\u00e9s de 14 extraordinarios espec\u00edmenes. Con salas dedicadas a temas diversos como los minerales, insectos(en el Vivarium podr\u00e1s observar entre otros seres vivos tar\u00e1ntulas e insectos palo) y conchas, siempre hay algo que descubrir en las colecciones permanentes.\r\n\r\nVisita la p\u00e1gina www.naturalsciences.be para m\u00e1s informaci\u00f3n sobre las exhibiciones temporales.\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"pt":{"name":"Museu das Ci\u00eancias Naturais","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"22\/06\/2022\r\nExplore a evolu\u00e7\u00e3o do ser humano e do seu corpo \u2013 do Sahelanthropus ao Homo sapiens, do embri\u00e3o ao adulto \u2013 tudo na nova Galeria do Ser Humano \u2013 a nossa evolu\u00e7\u00e3o, o nosso corpo.\r\nMas n\u00e3o \u00e9 tudo! Pode tamb\u00e9m descobrir a maior Galeria de Dinossauros da Europa, voltar no tempo na Galeria da Evolu\u00e7\u00e3o, com os seus 1000 esp\u00e9cimes, mergulhar em conjunto com os gigantescos lagartos marinhos do Cret\u00e1ceo na Sala dos Mosassauros, embarcar num safari urbano em BiodiverCITY e descobrir a hist\u00f3ria do museu atrav\u00e9s de 14 \u201ccap\u00edtulos\u201d simb\u00f3licos de 250 anos de Ci\u00eancias Naturais. Por \u00faltimo, as salas dedicadas aos Minerais, aos Insetos (com um viveiro, onde tar\u00e2ntulas, bichos-pau e outros vos far\u00e3o tremer) e aos Moluscos convencer-vos-\u00e3o que h\u00e1 sempre algo a descobrir nas nossas cole\u00e7\u00f5es permanentes.\r\nNavegue no site www.sciencesnaturelles.be para mais informa\u00e7\u00f5es sobre as exposi\u00e7\u00f5es tempor\u00e1rias","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null},"cn":{"name":"Mus\u00e9um des Sciences Naturelles","address_street_name":"Rue Vautier","address_street_number":"29","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@naturalsciences.be","website":"http:\/\/www.naturalsciences.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 627 42 11","phone_booking":"+32 2 627 42 34","address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue Vautier, 29","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"","description_print":"","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":8,"location":{"lat":50.83650849,"lon":4.37649387},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-07-21T01:35:45+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:13+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels.imgix.net\/661f683579f7d07025109054ab71c2213df82c0e.jpg","width":2480,"height":3508,"ratio":0.71,"translations":{"fr":{"title":"T. rex","copyright":"Mus\u00e9um des Sciences naturelles"},"nl":{"title":"T. rex","copyright":"Museum voor Natuurwetenschappen"},"en":{"title":"T. rex","copyright":"Museum of Natural Sciences"}}}],"dates":[{"day":"2021-10-13","doors":null,"start":"09:30:00","end":"17: